From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11, winewayland: Owned windows (Unreal's floating editors) above their owner, on the taskbar, hidden and shown with it.

* win32u, winex11: Owned windows hide and come back with their owner, as on Windows.

Unreal Engine's floating editor windows (owned by the main window, no taskbar button) were lost
after the desktop's "show desktop" and a restore of the main window, most of all on a second
monitor:
- winex11 turned the window manager's iconify of an owned window into SC_MINIMIZE: Windows' shell
  minimizes taskbar windows only, owned ones hide with their owner (SW_PARENTCLOSING). Minimized
  on their own they had no taskbar button to come back, and Wine minimized them again when the
  window manager restored them with the owner. The window manager's iconify of an owned window
  no longer minimizes it.
- ShowWindow showed the windows an owner hid when minimized only through DefWindowProc's
  SC_RESTORE and SC_MAXIMIZE; Windows does it in ShowWindow, whoever restores. Unreal Engine
  handles SC_RESTORE itself with ShowWindow(SW_RESTORE): its hidden floating windows never came
  back. show_window now shows them when the owner is shown again from minimized.

* winewayland: The toplevel of a window's owner is its xdg_toplevel parent.

Under Wayland, Unreal Engine's floating editor windows (owned by the main window) were toplevels
of their own: the main editor window could be raised above them, and the desktop showed them as
separate windows. On Windows owned windows stay above their owner, and winex11 tells window
managers so with WM_TRANSIENT_FOR. The toplevel of the owner is now set as the parent of an owned
window's toplevel (xdg_toplevel.set_parent), each time the window changes and the owner's
toplevel is another one.

* winex11: Owned windows with WS_EX_APPWINDOW are transient for their group.

Unreal Engine's floating editor windows (Material Editor, Niagara, Message Log) are owned by the
main window and have WS_EX_APPWINDOW: on Windows each has a taskbar button, grouped under the
application, and stays above the main window. winex11 made them transient for the owner and of
the dialog type: KDE Plasma's taskbar hides windows transient for another one, so a floating
window minimized with its own button could not be brought back, and KWin placed it again over its
owner (on the first monitor) when it was shown again. Such windows are now normal windows,
transient for the root window in the owner's group: ICCCM makes them transient for the group, so
window managers keep them above the owner, and taskbars show them. The window manager's iconify of
them minimizes them again (0028 kept it from owned windows without a taskbar button only).

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index fa7fce1..f71a581 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5013,6 +5013,13 @@ static BOOL show_window( HWND hwnd, INT cmd )
         }
     }
 
+    /* As Windows does in ShowWindow: an owner shown again from minimized shows the windows it hid
+     * when minimized, whoever restores it. Applications restoring with ShowWindow themselves,
+     * past DefWindowProc's SC_RESTORE (Unreal Engine), lost them. */
+    if ((style & WS_MINIMIZE) && !(style & WS_CHILD) && cmd != SW_HIDE && cmd != SW_MINIMIZE &&
+        cmd != SW_SHOWMINIMIZED && cmd != SW_SHOWMINNOACTIVE && cmd != SW_FORCEMINIMIZE)
+        NtUserShowOwnedPopups( hwnd, TRUE );
+
     switch(cmd)
     {
     case SW_HIDE:
